  "basis": "The task requires identifying the state with the highest GDP from the provided dashboard to route it to the follow-up workflow. The dashboard is a choropleth map titled 'Choropleth Map of GDP by State'. The legend indicates that darker colors correspond to higher GDP values (the scale goes from pale yellow at the top to dark red at the bottom). Visually, Kentucky is shaded in the darkest maroon color, which is darker than the bright red of Nebraska and the pale yellow of New Mexico. Although the specific numeric values on the map are small, the relative shading clearly places Kentucky in the highest category among the three options. This aligns with the visual evidence that Kentucky has the highest GDP.",
